Figure 5 illustrates Nano-11's ability to facilitate antigen transport to draining lymph nodes and target migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs). Flow cytometry plots and bar graphs show that Nano-11 significantly increases the mean fluorescence intensity of ovalbumin (OVA) within antigen-presenting cells (APCs) in the draining lymph nodes compared to soluble OVA or aluminum hydroxide (AH), especially on day 2. A higher percentage of OVA-positive cells are identified as MigDCs when antigen is formulated with Nano-11, indicating enhanced and more specific delivery to these immunopotentiating cells.